BRACS 2 [63] for breast cancer subtyping.
BRACS comprises 547 WSIs and 4,539 regions of interest extracted from those slides. Each WSI and corresponding ROI has been annotated based on the consensus of three board-certified pathologists, ensuring high-quality and reliable labeling. The dataset covers three primary lesion categories-benign, malignant, and atypical-which are further subtyped into seven diagnostic classes: Normal, Pathological Benign, Usual Ductal Hyperplasia, Flat Epithelial Atypia, Atypical Ductal Hyperplasia , Ductal Carcinoma In Situ, and Invasive Carcinoma.

