2.2. Supervised Finetuning
Supervised Finetuning (SFT) plays a key role in enhancing the instruction-following (Mishra et al., 2021; Sanh et al., 2021; Wei et al., 2022) and reasoning capabilities (Lambert et al., 2024). For a pretrained auto-regressive model with a fixed vocabulary V x and a labeled dataset D , SFT maximizes the likelihood: ˆ θ = arg max θ ∑ N i =1 log p θ ( y ( i ) | x ( i ) ) . This process retains the model's pretrained knowledge while aligning its outputs with task-specific objectives, typically using cross-entropy loss on the target tokens:
